$ uneffect check --evidence fixtures/contracts/loop-invariant-not-preserved.ts
# The invariant holds on entry but one iteration of the body breaks it.

error contract/invariant fixtures/contracts/loop-invariant-not-preserved.ts:7 in countByTwo
  message: `invariant i >= 0 && i <= n` is not preserved by one iteration of the loop body
  7 |   while (i < n) {
    |   ^
  rule: an iteration that starts with the invariant and the loop guard true must end with the invariant true
  counterexample: n@loop = 1, i@loop = 0
  state: n = n@loop = 1, i = i@loop + 2 = 2
  still holds: i@loop >= 0 && i@loop <= n@loop (0 >= 0 && 0 <= 1), i@loop < n@loop (0 < 1)
  fails: invariant i >= 0 && i <= n breaks at i <= n, which evaluates to 2 <= 1
  hint: establish the invariant before the loop and restore it in the body, or weaken it until both hold

1 error(s), 0 warning(s)

evidence:
